  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Smallpox, a contagious affliction, killed about three in ten of its sufferers and an estimated 300 million in the 20th century. An early safeguard, deliberately implanting matter from its sores in the healthy, was practised in China by the 16th century and reached England in 1721. The procedure itself could cause grave sickness or death, if less frequently than natural smallpox."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        391.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Rustic lore held that milkmaids with cowpox, a mild ailment of livestock, were immune to smallpox. In 1774 Benjamin Jesty, a Dorset farmer, employed cowpox to protect his wife and two sons. On 14 May 1796 Edward Jenner, a provincial practitioner, inserted fluid from a milkmaid's cowpox sore into a scratch on eight-year-old James Phipps."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        303.46141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        382.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 1 July 1796 Jenner exposed the boy to smallpox; no symptoms ensued. In 1797 the Royal Society declined to publish his paper, judging his evidence unconvincing. In June 1798 he privately funded his book, the Inquiry, with supplementary cases. The word vaccine derives from the Latin vacca, cow."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        195.96141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        294.96141732283473
      ],
      "text": "Jenner was not the idea's originator. His contribution was a test, with results accessible in print, so other doctors could replicate and disseminate the technique. By today's standards, experimentation on a child without informed consent would be unethical. Jenner died on 26 January 1823, with smallpox far from eliminated."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.46141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        187.46141732283473
      ],
      "text": "In 1967 the WHO launched an intensified, concerted campaign to eradicate smallpox. The last naturally occurring case was diagnosed in Somalia on 26 October 1977. On 8 May 1980 the World Health Assembly formally declared the world free of smallpox, the only human disease ever wiped out. That pronouncement came almost 184 years after Phipps was vaccinated."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "天花，一种传染性的疾病，夺去了约三成患者的生命，并且估计有3亿人在20世纪丧命。一种早期的防护手段，是有意把天花脓疮中的物质植入健康人体内，到16世纪，中国已在施行这种方法，1721年又传入英国。这种做法本身可能导致严重的疾病或死亡，尽管不如自然天花那样频繁。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        429.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "乡间传说认为，挤奶女工若得过牛痘这种牲畜的轻微病症，就对天花免疫。1774年，本杰明·杰斯蒂，一位多塞特郡农夫，使用牛痘来保护他的妻子和两个儿子。1796年5月14日，爱德华·詹纳，一位地方执业医师，将取自一名挤奶女工牛痘疮的液体，注入8岁的詹姆斯·菲普斯的一道划痕中。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        340.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        420.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1796年7月1日，詹纳让这个男孩接触天花；任何症状都没有随之出现。1797年，皇家学会拒绝去发表他的论文，认为他的证据缺乏说服力。1798年6月，他私人出资出版了他的著作《探究》，书中附上了补充病例。表示疫苗的英文词源自拉丁语的vacca，意思是牛。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        252.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        332.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "詹纳并不是这一想法的首创者。他的贡献是一项试验，其结果在已出版的书籍中可以获得，以便其他医生能够复制并传播这项技术。按今天的标准，拿孩子做实验在没有取得知情同意的情况下，属于不道德行为。詹纳于1823年1月26日去世，那时天花还远未被消除。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        163.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        243.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "1967年，世界卫生组织发起了一场强化、共同筹划的运动，要根除天花。最后一例自然发生的病例于1977年10月26日在索马里确诊。1980年5月8日，世界卫生大会正式宣布全世界已摆脱天花，天花也成为迄今唯一被彻底消灭的人类疾病。那一宣告，出现在菲普斯接种疫苗之后的近184年。"
    }
  ],
